00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.230
But, you know,
I'm happy to be here, of course.

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.765 align:start size:94% position:6%
-As we saw in the clip,
not only are you the directo

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:15.802
of this film,
you interview yourself, I guess.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.669 line:92%
You are listed as a fanboy

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:21.841
This is a band that you have
loved for a very long time

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you --
Have you been surprised

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
over the years that more peopl
didn't know them?

00:02:25.578 --> 00:02:27.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or is that what
you've come to expect?

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I come to expect it because
as I said in the clip,

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.286 size:81% position:41%
I was like 5 years old
when I saw them on TV.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:38.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
But in a pre-Internet age,
as we remember, um,

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:41.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was very difficult
to get information on bands,

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:43.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, beyond what might be
in a magazine

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.831 line:92%
or on the radio or on the TV

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
Before the Internet
and before Spotify

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:48.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
having somebody's
entire discography,

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:50.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was quite difficult
to pin bands down.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:54.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they were a band that kep
coming back into my life.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:57.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
And as that happened
more and more frequently,

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
I became
more and more obsessed.

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
They went from
being a riddle to me

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
to being, like,
a full-on obsession.

00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.817 line:92%
So I think in the last 20 years,

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've become, you know,
not just a fan,

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
but, you know, that kind o
evangelist with a band

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:14.561
where you're grabbing anybod
within your eye view to say,

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:17.897
"Hey, have you ever heard
Sparks? Listen to this!"

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:21.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talk about the technology
that wasn't available to u

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
as music fans
when we were growing up,

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:27.740
but you did use
the modern technology of Twitter

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.076 line:92%
to make contact with these guys.

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:31.444 line:92%
-Well, actually, bizarrely

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:34.280 line:92%
on one of my frequent marathon

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:36.316 align:start size:94% position:6%
of making somebody
in the same room

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
as me listen to Sparks...
[ Laughs ]

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:41.621
I suddenly thought, after having
been a big fan of them,

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
I never, like,
followed them on Twitter.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:46.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I said, "I wonder if Sparks
have a Twitter profile."

00:03:46.526 --> 00:03:50.530
And I looked at it, and it said,
"Sparks follows you,"

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.298 line:92%
which was so shocking to m

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:54.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
like, some artists --

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're very enigmatic,
Ron and Russell from Sparks,

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:59.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
a bit like Kate Bush
or David Bowie.

00:03:59.138 --> 00:04:01.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
And all of those people,
you don't imagine

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.675 line:92%
they live on planet Earth.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:05.445 size:78% position:39%
So then I immediately
direct-messaged them.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, first,
I followed them back,

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then I direct-messaged the
and said,

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Is this really the band?
I'm such a huge fan."

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:15.121
And Russell, the lead singer
messaged me back and said,

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:16.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, we're big fans
of your films."

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:19.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then within --
And then on top of that,

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.627 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I was in Los Angeles.

00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:21.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
So then it was
the weird thing of like,

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:24.497 size:88% position:44%
"Oh, they're only like
15 minutes' drive away."

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:27.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so within about 32 hours
I was having breakfast

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:31.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the two of them
at their house, which was wild

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, these guys,
as you mentioned,

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.040 size:78% position:39% line:92%
they're so enigmatic.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.809 size:75% position:38%
They're so stylized.
They're so unique.

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:39.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
Were you worried
that a lot of people

00:04:39.579 --> 00:04:43.616
when they first saw a traile
would think this was a ban

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:47.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
you had made up
like, say, Spinal Tap?

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:48.721 line:92%
-I mean, I think in a weird wa

00:04:48.721 --> 00:04:50.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's a good way
to go into the film.

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.158
I think a lot of people --
One thing I want to stress

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
is you do not have to be
a fan of the band to enjoy it.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:57.163
And I think, in a weird way,
if you've never heard them

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
before, it's quite a good wa
to see the movie.

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:03.503
And there are definitely som
people who saw it at festivals

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:06.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
who spent half
of the duration thinking,

00:05:06.072 --> 00:05:08.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wow. This is like
a really elaborate prank.

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:09.742 line:92%
How did he do all this archive?"

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:11.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like it's some kind
of Banksy thing.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:12.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I was going
to say actually --

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:13.613 line:92%
I wanted to say to you actuall

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:16.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I did an article for
Rotten Tomatoes the other da

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:19.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I listed my 10 favorit
music documentaries.

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.621 line:92%
And the top nine were all real

00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:23.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the number-10
wild-card choice

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
was "The Blue Jean Committee
Gentle and Soft"

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Documentary Now!"
I'm not kidding.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:31.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're very --
Thank you for putting us

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:33.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
in what I'm sure
is good company.

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean -- So, I mean,
it is a nice way to see it

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.772
because I think for a lot
of people who watched it -

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
And when I was editing
the movie,

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:44.010
I kept road-testing it wit
friends during the pandemic.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:47.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
And usually I sort out friends
who'd never heard of them.

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they all had
the same reaction.

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:50.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
They said,
"It is like sort of what --"

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:54.020
If you've never heard of the
before, it's like watching

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:56.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
a secret history of music
open up to you."

00:05:56.789 --> 00:06:00.360 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's kind of, you know --
But they're very real.

00:06:00.360 --> 00:06:02.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You also must --
As a documentary filmmaker

00:06:02.595 --> 00:06:03.796 line:92%
obviously, you pick the subject,

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:06.733
but you must,
as you're putting it together --

00:06:06.733 --> 00:06:08.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's such
great archival footage

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
thanks to the fact
that they were so unique.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:15.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
You must fall in love with the
as a director in a way

00:06:15.608 --> 00:06:19.979
that you had also fallen
in love with them as a fan

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:21.114 line:92%
-Yeah, I mean, they're so --

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:23.616
I had gotten to know them
after the Twitter thing.

00:06:23.616 --> 00:06:25.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a sort of --
You know, maybe back two years

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:29.389 size:88% position:44%
before it occurred to me
to make the documentary.

00:06:29.389 --> 00:06:31.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew what they were like
in person,

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:33.259
and the thing that I found
very endearing about them

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:35.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that they were
never, like, off the clock

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:38.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so there is a thing
that I guess --

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:40.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, watching this archive
and knowing them,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:41.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
there is this thing
where the line

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:43.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
between Ron and Russell
as brothers

00:06:43.936 --> 00:06:46.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the band
is just permanently blurred.

00:06:46.639 --> 00:06:49.609 size:78% position:39%
And I feel like they,
you know just, like,

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.444 size:88% position:44% line:92%
are sort of Sparks 24/7.

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:54.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there's something
really admirable about tha

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:57.150 line:92%
because they are the exception

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:59.051 align:start size:94% position:6%
in terms of
"don't meet your heroes."

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:02.555
You know, they're exactly
what you want them to be.

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the fact that
they're sort of so normal

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:06.592 line:92%
makes them kind of even weirder.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:07:07.460 --> 00:07:10.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know exactly
what you're talking about.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.264 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Hey. Congrats again.

00:07:11.264 --> 00:07:14.200
It's so wonderful, and I do hope
that we see you again

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
soon over here in the States
-Thank you.

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:19.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll be back
with some essential work.

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:22.308
-That would be very nice.
We would appreciate that.

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:26.179 size:78% position:39%
"The Sparks Brothers"
in theaters tomorrow.

